{
  "slug": "latio-secure-supply-chain-skills",
  "name": "Latio Secure Supply Chain Skills",
  "type": "plugin",
  "description": "Audit and take action to secure your repository against supply chain misconfigurations and malware.",
  "longDescription": "Ships **1 skill** and **18 commands**.\n\n- **Skills** (1): `supply-chain-hardening` (Use this skill when the user asks to \"harden supply chain\", \"secure dependencies\", \"pin versions\", \"audit packages\", \"secure…)\n- **Commands** (18): `audit-credentials` (Find long-lived tokens, hardcoded secrets, and credentials that should be rotated or replaced), `audit-supply-chain` (Run a full supply chain security audit across all domains), `harden-actions` (Pin GitHub Actions to SHAs, fix permissions, and flag dangerous triggers), `harden-ai-ml` (Fix unsafe model deserialization and harden AI/ML model usage), `harden-containers` (Pin base images by digest, enforce non-root, and harden Dockerfiles), `harden-credentials` (Scan for leaked secrets, set up pre-commit hooks, and harden credential hygiene), `harden-iac` (Pin Terraform modules, check state security, and flag dangerous provisioners), `harden-ide-extensions` (Audit IDE extensions and secure developer tool configs), and 10 more\n\nInstalls with `claude plugin install latio-secure-supply-chain-skills@claude-community` from `latiotech/secure-supply-chain-skills`.",
